Inferno/riscv64 native kernel (QEMU -M virt)

Build (from macOS host with KenC tools on PATH):

	export PATH=$ROOT/MacOSX/arm64/bin:$PATH ROOT=$ROOT
	cd os/virt
	rm -f ivirt   # force relink after lib changes
	mk SYSTARG=os OBJTYPE=riscv64 SHELLTYPE=sh INIT=virtinit install
	./smoke.sh

Kernel: Inferno/riscv64/bin/ivirt (jl -H5 -T0x80000000).
Init: os/init/virtinit.b rooted as /osinit.dis.

Notes
- KenC host is LP64; target Inferno/riscv64 is LLP64 (ulong/usize 32-bit)
  like Inferno/amd64.  jc stack args must pad to 8 (utils/jc/swt.c Aarg2 →
  SZ_VLONG, like 6c); else multi-arg snprint/print mis-reads slots.
  One-int-per-snprint call sites remain defensive.  Tk menu !reshape /
  ptr / cursor strings must also use one int per sprint (multi-int tkwreq
  corrupted geometry → menus never mapped).
- jl float literals: Ieee in utils/jc/i.out.h must be two 32-bit words
  (int, not host long).  With sizeof(long)==8, ADATA for 10.0 etc. was
  emitted as zeros → dtoa/g_fmt hung; Limbo %g follows amd64 snprint path.
- DRAMSIZE is 256MiB (mem.h / QEMU -m 256); archconfinit must use it
  (was hard-coded 128MiB → half the RAM invisible to pools).
- poolsizeinit must use uvlong for nb*pcnt (LLP64 ulong wraps; image
  pool was ~30MiB instead of ~150MiB).
- Kernel profiling: #K (devkprof); echo startclr/stop/dump >/dev/kpctl.
  clockintr samples ur->pc; cycles() reads mcycle (not HZ ticks).
  SMOKE_KEEP_LOG=/tmp/log ./os/virt/stress.sh keeps the serial log.
- Display: gscreen draws directly into the ramfb buffer (no soft→fb
  memcpy — that copy dominated Bounce). Soft cursor overlays with
  under[] save/restore; flushmemscreen only repairs the glyph when
  the dirty rect hits it or the hotpoint moved. cursorproc: one
  compose per wakeup (no busy-while). Lock-free (never waits on
  drawlock). play.sh uses -display cocoa,show-cursor=on.
- Virtio tablet: used-ring drain needs coherence before reading usedent;
  recycling a garbage id permanently stuck the pointer after Bounce/QMP
  floods. Nbuf=256, reclaim-all on bad id, drain-until-quiet.
- Bounce (stock Limbo): no-WM tkclient !reshape used to map di.r (full
  display) ignoring Required size → act ~640×480, walls on boundary,
  “no intersection!”. tkclient now honors the reshape rect. Keep Bounce
  unmodified; fix windowing/runtime, not the game.
- KenC fdlibm: fabs/atan2 must not rely on __HI(x) mutating a double
  parameter (stack image updated, FP reg stale → NaN). Use compare/-x
  and return -z. Broken atan2(-1,1) made stock Bounce print
  “no intersection!” after the reshape fix.
- Busy Dis (Bounce): stock game; sys->sleep(ms) can stick in acquire
  while Tk_cmd holds the Dis VM. virtinit iptimer spins sleep(0) so
  wmstress stays fair without changing Bounce. vmachine/flushmemscreen
  clockcheck() keep soft timers moving under load.
- BusyGC throttled (emu-style) + skip pushrun if addrun set (avoids
  panic: pushrun addrun under wm load).
- KSTACK 32KiB (was 8KiB): trap+draw on process stack; Cocoa mouse
  otherwise overflowed → cause 0x2 at heap/BSS (execute non-text).
- TCP diag prints (%I.%d → %I.%d …): KenC LP64 one-arg-per-print only;
  multi-arg print faulted in utflen (cause 0x5 tval 0xde) on RST → "hung".
- Softscreen + optional ramfb (fw_cfg); virtio input/kbd, rng, blk, net.
- ndb/dns + ndb/cs bind #s on /net (default).  dns udpport() must not use
  Dial->announce (that walks /net/cs and deadlocks with dns).
- Local A records: dns.b dblooka() reads dom=/sys= ip= from /lib/ndb/local.
- dns readservers uses dblooknet when /dev/sysname is set (virtinit writes "virt").
- Toolbar: apply join "rect" in waitctl; /lib/wmsetup prints TB-OK + COLORS-OK.
- Virtio input: drain in kproc (not IRQ); mousetrack must not call drawactive.
- /dev/pointer: KenC-safe sprint; decref on close; set /dev/sysname in virtinit.
- Rooted desktop: plumber, acme, charon, wm/man, view/ftree/edit/tetris,
  wm/{task,rt,deb,coffee}.  Coffee needs /icons/bigdelight + coffee0–5 bit/mask.
  Lean lucida/lucm + /fonts/charon (latin1 bits only).
  Lean /man/1 (~22 pages) + convcs utf8/latin1.
  Charon start: file:/services/webget/start.html (lean, no GIF).
  Plumbing: edits→acme, URLs→charon, name(sec)→wm/man.
  Software cursor (os/port/swcursor + screenvirt); /dev/cursor wired.
  Smoke: TASKPROG-OK, ACME/MAN/CHARON-LIVE-OK, CHARON-HTTP-OK (host
  :8765), ROOT-APPS.  QEMU -m 256; image_pool_pcnt 60.  dumpstack walks
  kstack; /prog status uses KenC-safe snprint (wm/task).  Rooted
  strinttab/html for Charon/HTML.  KenC-safe tcpstate/devip local+remote.

Interactive QEMU (GUI window, not -nographic):

	./os/virt/play.sh
	# Or: hostfwd + FAT FS-OK image + echoes (see play.sh).  Bare qemu
	# without hostfwd prints TCP-IN-FAIL timeout / FS-FAIL content.

Acme: needs writable /tmp (memfs in virtinit → TMP-OK) and /mnt/acme.
  Disk.init creates /tmp/X*.acme; without memfs acme exits immediately.
  Rebuild appl/acme together (stale gui.dis vs acme.dis → link typecheck).
  Heavysmoke ACME-LIVE uses makedrawcontext (no wmsrv) so pointer/plumb
  warnings are expected; menu Acme under wm is the real check.
Memory monitor: /dev/memory via poolread (KenC-safe 11-digit fields);
  MEMORY-OK at boot.  Empty bars were poolmax underflow: static cursize
  started at 31MB while virt poolsize() set maxsize ~25MB → huge 7th
  field broke wm/memory's fixed columns.  cursize now starts 0.
  Recopy dis/wm/memory.dis after limbo.
Dis stress (virtinit + ./os/virt/stress.sh):
  CMD-STRESS-OK — file ops + mkdir + wc/grep/tail/… under /tmp (memfs).
  memfs Create sets QTDIR before Qidhash.add.  ulong/usize are LLP64
  (32-bit) like Inferno/amd64 + KenC; FPcontrol is plain C.  memset
  must MOVWU the count (64-bit MOV smeared stack garbage → RAM end).
  KenC F28–F31 (0.0/0.5/1.0/2.0) inited in l.s like Power fp.s; other
  float literals via jl ADATA.  Limbo %g/%e/%f uses snprint→gfltconv→dtoa
  (amd64 path).  MATH-OK / REAL-OK / CMD-STRESS calc-ok.
  WM-STRESS-OK — live+kill including ftree (/tmp, no nested plumber) and
  deb (/icons/tk/debug/*).  Charon charsets include windows-1252.
  Acme/man/charon in heavysmoke.  Ends with DIS-STRESS-OK.
